No, you misunderstand. It's not "a word that has a full stop in it". It IS =
two words. The fact that they are written together with a full stop doesn't=
 change that fact. We can write "la djan. klama lo zarci mu'i lo nu vo'a se=
 jersi .ii" as "ladjan.klama lozarci mu'ilonuvo'asejersi.ii' and it's still=
 completely unambiguous (although a pain for humans to read) with the full =
stops indicating the one MUST pause there, otherwise it means something els=
e.
